[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |      # Gated / private — supply an HF access token.
[agent:result]  |      m = mr.hf_download("meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B", hf_token="hf_xxx")
[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |      # Multi-quant repo — pick exactly one variant.
[agent:result]  |      m = mr.hf_download(
[agent:result]  |          "unsloth/Kimi-K2.6-GGUF", selected_variants=["UD-Q4_K_XL"]
[agent:result]  |      )
[agent:result]  |      ```
[agent:result]  |
[agent:result]  |      Parameters:
[agent:result]  |          hugging_face_model_id: HF repo id (``owner/repo``) or full HuggingFace URL.
[agent:result]  |          hf_token: Optional HuggingFace access token; required for gated/private repos.
[agent:result]  |          selected_formats: Weight-format keys to download (``safetensors``, ``pytorch``,
[agent:result]  |              ``tensorflow``, ``flax``, ``gguf``, ``onnx``, ``openvino``, ``coreml``,
[agent:result]  |              ``tflite``). When omitted, the backend picks one with the precedence
[agent:result]  |              safetensors > pytorch > tensorflow > flax > … so multi-format repos don't
[agent:result]  |              pull every copy of the same weights.
[agent:result]  |          selected_variants: GGUF / unsloth quantisation tags to keep
[agent:result]  |              (``Q4_K_M``, ``UD-Q4_K_XL``, ``BF16``, …). Acts as a sub-filter — files
[agent:result]  |              with a quant tag are only downloaded if their tag is in the list. Files
[agent:result]  |              without a tag (root README, config, …) are unaffected.
[agent:result]  |          selected_filenames: Explicit per-file allowlist. When non-empty this
[agent:result]  |              overrides ``selected_formats`` / ``selected_variants`` and the backend
[agent:result]  |              downloads exactly these paths.
[agent:result]  |          timeout: Maximum seconds to wait for the import to reach a terminal state.
[agent:result]  |          poll_interval: Seconds between status polls.
